   "body": "**Adversarial review (Opus 5.5, reviewer subagent, round 1): REQUEST CHANGES** — head 01b59a7f\n\n1. **High** — `App/SwiftHFR/Root/RootTabsView.swift:122`: the new `// Differences: GAP-1450 …` line is 144 characters long. CI runs `swiftlint lint --strict` (`ci.yml:28`), so the required lint job fails (`line_length` error at 122:1, reproduced locally). **Fix:** wrap the comment.\n\n2. **Medium** — `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/FavoritesPresentation.swift:28-34`: `effectiveLayout` forces `showsCollapsedSections` on but leaves `showsEmptySections` alone, and that stays `showsCollapsedSections(setting) && mode == .flagsAndFavorites` (`FavoritesOptionsModel.swift:113`).\n   - Legacy at 87fe0d1c: `shouldShowEmptyFavoriteSections = showsAllFavoriteSections && tab == \"0\"` (`:496-497`); in the flat sort `showsAllFavoriteSections == showsCategoriesOnDemand` (`:492-494`).\n   - Failing scenario: \"Drapeaux & Favoris\", flat sort, `FavoritesShowCollapsedSections` at its default `false` (`:448`), tap the on-demand item. Legacy lists the empty categories (`:589`); the PR drops them. The ledger row says \"même règle\", which is not true. The pure test only covers `showsEmptySections: false` with an empty mode.\n   - **Fix:** under on-demand, set `showsEmptySections` to `mode == .flagsAndFavorites` (pass the mode in, or compute it in the model). Pin it with a test in each mode.\n\n3. **Low** — `RootTabsView.swift:155`: legacy's visible label is « Afficher les catégories » (`:817`); « Afficher toutes les catégories » is only its accessibility label (`:846`). Use the visible label, or stop calling it \"legacy labels\" in the PR and the ledger row.\n\n4. **Detail** — legacy plays `AppHaptics.impact(.light)` on this button (`:812`); the port plays nothing and does not list that as a difference. Add the haptic or document why it is left out.\n\n**Verified:** worktree at 01b59a7f; `swiftlint lint --strict` on the changed files (finding 1); `ledger.py check-body` on the PR body (1 block ok); legacy read at `Favorites.swift` :445-497, :575-605, :654-662, :796-846 @ 87fe0d1c; stored properties set in `init` do not trigger `didSet`; the reset fires through `reloadSettings()`; `displayedGroups` and `allSectionsHidden` are computed and observed; nothing is persisted. **Not run:** app tests (cannot build on Linux).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
